# --- site-factory generated artifacts ---
# Audit and outreach outputs are third-party business data, and CLAUDE.md
# forbids committing client data. The generic `out` and `dist` rules above
# already match some of these by accident; these entries are anchored to the
# repo root and state the intent explicitly, so the behaviour survives any
# future edit to the framework blocks above.
/audit/
/outreach/
# Ingested prospect data: their photos, logo, reviews, address and the
# generated config built from them. Same category as the two above.
/prospects/

# Real lead data. Ignore the whole category — every lead CSV, current and
# future — and re-admit only the tracked fixture. Naming individual files here
# meant each new lead CSV was tracked by default until someone remembered to
# add it; this inverts that default.
/data/*.csv
!/data/businesses.sample.csv
